266
00:22:25,460 --> 00:22:27,580
We are begging you, King Rick!

267
00:22:27,900 --> 00:22:30,337
It took some time for
the truth to get out!

268
00:22:30,420 --> 00:22:33,120
As Muke Toys, we were unable to speak up!

269
00:22:33,420 --> 00:22:34,540
No, I cannot.

270
00:22:35,240 --> 00:22:36,840
Please, respect my wishes.

271
00:22:40,720 --> 00:22:45,540
Even with the misunderstanding
absolved, I cannot return to the throne.

272
00:22:46,220 --> 00:22:50,300
But you're the only ruler worthy
to lead, Dressrosa! He's right!

273
00:22:50,620 --> 00:22:52,640
We're done with all this violence!

274
00:22:52,940 --> 00:22:54,120
Please, King Rick!

275
00:22:54,440 --> 00:22:56,757
We share your vision of a peaceful future!

276
00:22:56,840 --> 00:22:58,520
We beg you! Hmm?

277
00:23:06,600 --> 00:23:07,980
Hold your pleas.

278
00:23:09,880 --> 00:23:13,000
Under pressure, the Rick
family ideals shatter.

279
00:23:13,440 --> 00:23:16,220
Has that not been proven by now?

280
00:23:18,860 --> 00:23:20,720
We don't care if we fall.

281
00:23:21,580 --> 00:23:25,157
For the chance of being a bloodless
nation, we're happy to risk it.

282
00:23:25,240 --> 00:23:29,711
We want a king who will resist wars,
and we know you're the man for the job.

283
00:23:30,140 --> 00:23:30,970
That's right.

284
00:23:31,053 --> 00:23:34,080
Even if it results in failure,
we'll take that chance.

285
00:23:35,400 --> 00:23:37,040
Who cares if we're poor?

286
00:23:37,300 --> 00:23:40,712
Just make Dressrosa a peaceful
kingdom like we used to be.

287
00:23:40,820 --> 00:23:44,180
Please, King Rick, listen
to the cries of your people.

288
00:23:45,080 --> 00:23:47,200
No one better suited to lead us.

289
00:23:54,640 --> 00:23:57,320
As the fighting king, I'm not used to this

290
00:23:58,560 --> 00:24:00,000
Huh? Elisabello?

291
00:24:01,740 --> 00:24:04,505
King Rick, please return
to the palace at once.

292
00:24:05,100 --> 00:24:07,857
There's a bunch of incoming calls
from our neighboring nations.

293
00:24:07,940 --> 00:24:09,257
They'd like to talk!

294
00:24:09,340 --> 00:24:10,840
But to me?

295
00:24:13,140 --> 00:24:13,970
Well,

296
00:24:14,053 --> 00:24:16,457
I took it upon myself to
get the word out to people

297
00:24:16,540 --> 00:24:19,364
when I told them a King
Rick would be returning,

298
00:24:19,540 --> 00:24:21,540
they all seem overjoyed.

299
00:24:21,820 --> 00:24:23,300
The King of Prudence?

300
00:24:25,960 --> 00:24:29,417
Surely you haven't changed that
much in a mere decade, my friends.

301
00:24:29,500 --> 00:24:31,197
What happened to the old you?

302
00:24:31,280 --> 00:24:36,104
The man who'd give a firm stink-eye to
anyone even thinking about waging war, huh?

303
00:24:38,280 --> 00:24:40,260
They're all waiting on him.

304
00:24:43,300 --> 00:24:44,897
Come back to the throne.

305
00:24:44,980 --> 00:24:49,100
King of Miracles, Rick Doldo III!

306
00:24:50,080 --> 00:24:53,440
Your friend's a smart
man there, King Rick.

307
00:25:08,980 --> 00:25:11,937
This entire mess is Doflamingo's doing.

308
00:25:12,020 --> 00:25:14,257
I would hate to see you shoulder the

309
00:25:14,340 --> 00:25:17,340
responsibility alone for
the error in his judgment.

310
00:25:18,060 --> 00:25:20,480
That crooked pirate was unfit to rule.

311
00:25:20,660 --> 00:25:23,657
But thanks to a broken arrangement
with a bunch of convicts,

312
00:25:23,740 --> 00:25:25,916
the Seven Warlords system failed you.

313
00:25:26,200 --> 00:25:30,337
Sadly, Dressrosa was forced to pay
this price by the bloodstained hands.

314
00:25:30,420 --> 00:25:32,940
They lost the world government.

315
00:25:37,720 --> 00:25:39,014
People of the kingdom.

316
00:25:40,760 --> 00:25:43,340
and members of the royal family.

317
00:25:55,320 --> 00:25:57,240
On behalf of the government,

318
00:25:58,280 --> 00:26:03,140
allow me to offer my
most humble of apologies.

319
00:26:29,520 --> 00:26:33,740
With deep regret, we've done
you a terrible disservice.

320
00:26:36,540 --> 00:26:37,960
What's this about?

321
00:26:49,000 --> 00:26:51,960
Admiral Isho is actually kneeling?

322
00:26:52,620 --> 00:26:53,840
I'm shocked.

323
00:26:56,880 --> 00:26:58,360
Now this is wild.

324
00:26:58,700 --> 00:27:00,817
The Navy works directly
under the government,

325
00:27:00,900 --> 00:27:03,197
and one of their highly
respected officials?

326
00:27:03,280 --> 00:27:06,400
is on the ground apologizing to King Rick.

327
00:27:06,660 --> 00:27:08,895
What happened over there in Dressrosa?

328
00:27:09,000 --> 00:27:12,800
The fall of the heavenly demon
was due to some pirate alliance?

329
00:27:13,900 --> 00:27:14,920
Take notes!

330
00:27:15,120 --> 00:27:16,473
Don't miss any details!

331
00:27:17,020 --> 00:27:19,491
I've never seen anything like this before.

332
00:27:21,960 --> 00:27:27,800
The false prosperity of the mighty Dressrosa,
the unsavory secrets that they held.

333
00:27:28,160 --> 00:27:31,140
The downfall of Don Quixote Doflamingo,

334
00:27:31,400 --> 00:27:34,260
the world's most notorious
black market broker,

335
00:27:34,500 --> 00:27:38,680
and the Navy HQ Admiral
Fujitora's heartfelt prostration.

336
00:27:40,360 --> 00:27:43,860
All these truths have been
freed from the birdcage,

337
00:27:44,040 --> 00:27:49,680
and for better or worse,

338
00:27:50,100 --> 00:27:53,740
they have been unleashed
upon the entire world.

339
00:28:21,100 --> 00:28:24,300
The Navy Admiral is bowing to King Rick?

340
00:28:24,560 --> 00:28:26,384
Wow, they're recording it, too.

341
00:28:32,700 --> 00:28:34,200
Hey, look!

342
00:28:34,500 --> 00:28:36,206
That guy's an admiral, right?

343
00:28:36,420 --> 00:28:37,280
No way.

344
00:28:37,600 --> 00:28:38,780
This is a big deal.

345
00:28:39,220 --> 00:28:41,808
Something really nuts
happened in Dressrosa.

346
00:28:44,040 --> 00:28:47,000
Please raise your head, admiral.

347
00:28:51,620 --> 00:28:52,680
Come on, now.

348
00:28:53,560 --> 00:28:56,148
Do you truly wish for
the world to see this?

349
00:29:01,740 --> 00:29:04,280
My word, don't tell me.

350
00:29:06,040 --> 00:29:08,660
Is this why you did not engage Doflamingo?

351
00:29:13,700 --> 00:29:14,530
Fujitora.

352
00:29:14,613 --> 00:29:17,404
It was about time the
world found out the truth.

353
00:29:17,760 --> 00:29:21,348
So I took one mighty gamble and
let them do all the fighting.

354
00:29:21,700 --> 00:29:23,465
It was what needed to be done.

355
00:29:23,960 --> 00:29:27,697
How could we let that warlord do
whatever he pleased for all those years?

356
00:29:27,780 --> 00:29:30,898
Then swoop in here and start
preaching about justice.

357
00:29:31,160 --> 00:29:32,866
It doesn't sit right with me.

358
00:29:33,020 --> 00:29:35,432
We can't play hero for a problem we made.

359
00:29:41,700 --> 00:29:46,641
What we witnessed today was a kingdom that
came together and seized its own justice.

360
00:29:47,340 --> 00:29:51,337
You should be thanking the courageous
actions of pirates, gladiators,

361
00:29:51,420 --> 00:29:52,479
and your citizens.

362
00:29:53,320 --> 00:29:55,340
The arduous battle is over.

363
00:29:55,620 --> 00:29:56,940
I thank you all.

364
00:29:59,620 --> 00:30:01,420
I know it's been difficult.

365
00:30:03,160 --> 00:30:04,860
Anti-Doflamingo Force!

366
00:30:05,080 --> 00:30:06,460
Little King Rick Army!

367
00:30:06,960 --> 00:30:08,340
Kill, sir commander!

368
00:30:09,660 --> 00:30:11,820
Your operation is now complete.

369
00:30:15,640 --> 00:30:16,960
We're disbanded.

370
00:30:18,860 --> 00:30:19,690
Commander!

371
00:30:24,820 --> 00:30:27,440
Tank, the Navy must maintain face.

372
00:30:27,940 --> 00:30:30,234
The pirates and gladiators should hide.

373
00:30:30,460 --> 00:30:31,872
Take them to the palace.

374
00:30:32,460 --> 00:30:34,813
The same goes for anyone without a home.

375
00:30:35,060 --> 00:30:36,001
Can you do that?

376
00:30:36,280 --> 00:30:38,380
It'd be my pleasure, King Rick.

377
00:30:59,040 --> 00:30:59,870
So,

378
00:30:59,953 --> 00:31:03,097
you're telling me that that whole
mix up with Doflamingo leaving the

379
00:31:03,180 --> 00:31:07,780
Warlords was actually from some power
even higher than the lot of you?

380
00:31:14,600 --> 00:31:17,697
Want to explain how
that rat Doflamingo was

381
00:31:17,780 --> 00:31:20,192
able to manipulate the world to his will?

382
00:31:20,700 --> 00:31:22,860
This kind of malarkey needs to end,

383
00:31:23,000 --> 00:31:26,118
or else I'll be the
laughingstock of the entire Navy!

384
00:31:26,240 --> 00:31:28,700
Don't pull a stunt like that ever again.

385
00:31:29,120 --> 00:31:32,000
It would be wise to hold
your tongue, Admiral.

386
00:31:32,560 --> 00:31:35,320
Your honor is of no
concern to us right now.

387
00:31:36,120 --> 00:31:37,460
Don't get a big head.

388
00:31:37,600 --> 00:31:39,953
The Navy merely acts as our public face.

389
00:31:40,220 --> 00:31:43,985
Regardless, this whole affair was
placed in Cypher-Pole's hands.

390
00:31:44,160 --> 00:31:44,990
Ha!

391
00:31:45,073 --> 00:31:46,380
Cypher-Pole, you say?

392
00:31:47,260 --> 00:31:48,980
Let's lay out the facts here.

393
00:31:49,420 --> 00:31:53,077
Sounds like the Celestial Dragon's
puppet went right over your heads.

394
00:31:53,160 --> 00:31:55,117
Are you all really okay with that?

395
00:31:55,200 --> 00:31:57,440
Watch your insolent mouth, Sakasuki.

396
00:31:57,760 --> 00:32:00,120
Got anything to say about Kuzan? Hmm?

397
00:32:00,780 --> 00:32:05,960
How is someone as powerful as him allying
himself with Blackbeard of all people?

398
00:32:06,840 --> 00:32:09,920
The Navy's reputation is already sullied.

399
00:32:10,060 --> 00:32:12,860
That lackadaisical jackass
officially resigned.

400
00:32:13,520 --> 00:32:17,780
Who he chooses to partner with has
absolutely jacked to do with us.

401
00:32:18,180 --> 00:32:20,140
Five Elders! Fleet Admiral!

402
00:32:25,780 --> 00:32:27,900
I have urgent news.

403
00:32:28,120 --> 00:32:30,957
It's concerning the state
of the Don Quixote family.

404
00:32:31,040 --> 00:32:32,334
Doflamingo has fallen.

405
00:32:32,560 --> 00:32:35,017
Defeated by Straw Hat and Law's Alliance.

406
00:32:35,100 --> 00:32:39,740
But in the process, Tress Rossa was
reduced to rubble completely. Huh?

407
00:32:40,000 --> 00:32:40,860
That's absurd!

408
00:32:45,200 --> 00:32:46,340
I see.

409
00:32:46,720 --> 00:32:48,040
That damn boy.

410
00:32:51,220 --> 00:32:53,500
Sir, it doesn't end there.

411
00:33:08,200 --> 00:33:11,097
The broadcast transmission
that was sent from

412
00:33:11,180 --> 00:33:14,297
Desrosa quickly became
the talk of every country.

413
00:33:14,380 --> 00:33:19,297
There's breaking news, everybody
spreading like wildfire!

414
00:33:19,380 --> 00:33:21,897
It caused chaos amongst the underworld.

415
00:33:21,980 --> 00:33:27,817
Joker was defeated, your majesty—he
was the only weapon supplier we had.

416
00:33:27,900 --> 00:33:28,730
We'll

417
00:33:30,100 --> 00:33:32,117
announce our surrender at once.

418
00:33:32,200 --> 00:33:33,030
once

419
00:33:38,220 --> 00:33:40,520
The war is finally over!

420
00:33:42,900 --> 00:33:44,580
But we've already paid!

421
00:33:44,880 --> 00:33:45,900
We had a deal!

422
00:33:46,120 --> 00:33:47,960
Joker, you slimy bastard!

423
00:33:48,660 --> 00:33:51,340
The weapons are somewhere at Dressrosa!

424
00:33:51,540 --> 00:33:52,797
So is the Navy Admiral.

425
00:33:52,880 --> 00:33:53,997
Forget about it, man.

426
00:33:54,080 --> 00:33:56,517
So our sweet devil
fruit deal fell through?

427
00:33:56,600 --> 00:33:59,297
What's gonna happen to
my smile agreement, huh?

428
00:33:59,380 --> 00:34:02,380
If only those meddling
punks had showed up!

429
00:34:08,060 --> 00:34:09,080
Come on, Tsuru.

430
00:34:09,340 --> 00:34:10,837
You didn't need to set sail.

431
00:34:10,920 --> 00:34:11,750
I have this.

432
00:34:12,100 --> 00:34:15,157
Took the words right out of
my mouth, Inspector General.

433
00:34:15,240 --> 00:34:18,777
Well, I suppose you have been on
their trail for quite some time now.

434
00:34:18,860 --> 00:34:20,560
Yes, by your orders.

435
00:34:21,340 --> 00:34:23,260
Want a cracker? I'm good.

436
00:34:25,420 --> 00:34:26,920
Might I suggest this?

437
00:34:27,240 --> 00:34:29,240
Supreme is our special of the day.

438
00:34:30,320 --> 00:34:31,700
Huh? A thief!

439
00:34:31,900 --> 00:34:33,488
Get back here, you old bag!

440
00:34:34,060 --> 00:34:35,860
Now where'd that old lady go?

441
00:34:40,660 --> 00:34:43,580
Damn, just a kid. Where are you? Hey!

442
00:34:44,900 --> 00:34:47,940
Hey, they took out Dolpholingo. Not bad.

443
00:34:48,340 --> 00:34:50,693
I'm proud to call them generation mates.

444
00:35:03,480 --> 00:35:04,920
High Priest Aruge!

445
00:35:06,620 --> 00:35:08,140
High Priest Aruge!

446
00:35:11,640 --> 00:35:13,077
There's somebody up here!

447
00:35:13,160 --> 00:35:14,020
High Priest!

448
00:35:15,680 --> 00:35:17,180
Now that's just silly.

449
00:35:17,900 --> 00:35:19,357
Do you know where we are?

450
00:35:19,440 --> 00:35:22,322
A remote cloud island
where no one can bother us.

451
00:35:22,640 --> 00:35:24,522
Trust me when I say it's a bird.

452
00:35:36,940 --> 00:35:39,720
Whoa, whoa, the cojones on them two guys.

453
00:35:40,660 --> 00:35:44,457
Looks like our little pirate Pallies
are making a name for themselves.

454
00:35:44,540 --> 00:35:47,857
That means we'll be glomming Caesar
for ourselves, boys, capisce?

455
00:35:47,940 --> 00:35:49,360
Yes, father!

456
00:35:53,760 --> 00:35:56,466
That didn't take him
long to pull ahead of us.

457
00:35:56,580 --> 00:35:58,380
This is a huge triumph.

458
00:35:58,920 --> 00:36:01,857
Interesting, since Doflamingo's
got connections with Kaido.

459
00:36:01,940 --> 00:36:04,705
There's no way he's not
going to be pissed off.

460
00:36:05,060 --> 00:36:08,680
If this was intentional, they
just outed who they're after.

461
00:36:10,660 --> 00:36:12,540
One of the four emperors.

462
00:36:15,000 --> 00:36:17,529
Facing the king of the
beasts himself, huh?

463
00:36:19,200 --> 00:36:22,137
Well, at least our target
is different than theirs.

464
00:36:22,220 --> 00:36:25,540
It saves us the hassle of
wasting manpower on them.

465
00:36:26,300 --> 00:36:29,117
That still leaves
red-haired shanks all to us.

466
00:36:29,200 --> 00:36:34,217
We'll be able to keep focusing on that
goal or it even traveled to Drake who

467
00:36:34,300 --> 00:36:39,360
once made a name for himself by provoking
Kaido Do Flamingo killed your old man.

468
00:36:39,600 --> 00:36:40,600
How'd I not know?

469
00:36:48,020 --> 00:36:49,420
That's in the past now.

470
00:36:49,620 --> 00:36:51,917
I bear no grudge damn dude.

471
00:36:52,000 --> 00:36:53,200
You are ice cold

472
00:36:53,780 --> 00:36:55,400
Why not come help us?

473
00:36:56,120 --> 00:36:58,217
This needs to be reported to the big man.

474
00:36:58,300 --> 00:37:00,712
And something tells me he won't be happy!

475
00:37:01,260 --> 00:37:03,817
Master Kaino, you're not gonna like this.

476
00:37:03,900 --> 00:37:06,257
That schmuck Joker
screwed up a good thing.

477
00:37:06,340 --> 00:37:08,480
We won't be getting smiles anymore.

478
00:37:11,400 --> 00:37:13,340
Don't play dumb with me, Esho.

479
00:37:16,020 --> 00:37:18,737
Now you know damn well
what it means for a ranking

480
00:37:18,820 --> 00:37:21,467
official to admit an
oversight on this scale!

481
00:37:21,780 --> 00:37:24,604
Why didn't you think to
first report this to HQ?

482
00:37:26,860 --> 00:37:28,517
If I'd followed protocol,

483
00:37:28,600 --> 00:37:30,417
I have a feeling that the news would have

484
00:37:30,500 --> 00:37:32,897
come out with a bit of
a different spin on it.

485
00:37:32,980 --> 00:37:33,810
Huh?

486
00:37:33,893 --> 00:37:35,420
Care to repeat that?

487
00:37:40,860 --> 00:37:44,400
I believe the Seven Warlords
system should be abolished.

488
00:37:48,700 --> 00:37:54,040
Two years ago, I was there in person
when Crocodile's ruse was exposed.

489
00:37:55,400 --> 00:37:58,165
And the Navy couldn't do
a damn thing about it.

490
00:38:03,420 --> 00:38:05,857
If it weren't for the
Straw Hats back then,

491
00:38:05,940 --> 00:38:08,337
Alabasta would have
become a pirate nation,

492
00:38:08,420 --> 00:38:10,420
just like Dressrosa is now.

493
00:38:11,120 --> 00:38:15,649
But the government falsely declared
Crocodile's downfall was due to the Navy.

494
00:38:17,420 --> 00:38:20,220
If only I had a higher rank back then!

495
00:38:33,580 --> 00:38:34,780
I'll be damned.

496
00:38:35,780 --> 00:38:37,133
Fujitora really did it.

497
00:38:37,400 --> 00:38:38,280
Well done.

498
00:38:38,680 --> 00:38:43,327
I remember how frustrated both of us were
after what happened back in Alabasta.

499
00:38:43,920 --> 00:38:47,626
But this time, the Straw Hat's
achievement won't be covered up.

500
00:38:49,280 --> 00:38:52,357
It kind of feels like
retribution for that whole mess.

501
00:38:52,440 --> 00:38:53,437
I'll hand it to him.

502
00:38:53,520 --> 00:38:56,537
I couldn't pull this off when
I was in the same position.

503
00:38:56,620 --> 00:38:58,460
I'm completely astonished.

504
00:38:59,260 --> 00:39:00,340
We've got muffins.

505
00:39:00,660 --> 00:39:01,877
Shall I make some coffee?

506
00:39:01,960 --> 00:39:03,900
I said astonished, not famished.

507
00:39:05,380 --> 00:39:07,160
Hey, sis, we're hungry.

508
00:39:07,760 --> 00:39:08,590
Starby!

509
00:39:08,673 --> 00:39:10,077
You can have his share then.

510
00:39:10,160 --> 00:39:11,278
Anyone want coffee?

511
00:39:11,400 --> 00:39:13,576
You can't give coffee to kids, silly.

512
00:39:13,920 --> 00:39:15,060
I want a muffin.

513
00:39:15,440 --> 00:39:16,860
Where's Mr. Vegabunk?

514
00:39:17,000 --> 00:39:18,377
I think you mean Vegabunk.

515
00:39:18,460 --> 00:39:22,989
It'll take just a few more days before
we reach his lab, so hang tight, okay?

516
00:39:24,060 --> 00:39:24,980
Look at that.

517
00:39:25,260 --> 00:39:27,057
The captain's so good with kids.

518
00:39:27,140 --> 00:39:28,960
Man, I wish I were five.

519
00:39:29,260 --> 00:39:30,672
All right, enough, guys.

520
00:39:30,800 --> 00:39:32,717
There's still plenty of work to do.

521
00:39:32,800 --> 00:39:33,660
Yes, ma 'am.

522
00:39:33,840 --> 00:39:36,016
I love it when you scold me, captain.

523
00:39:52,740 --> 00:39:55,580
It's called damage
control, and it's common!

524
00:39:55,880 --> 00:39:59,817
Our superiors thought those pirates would
help maintain balance in this world.

525
00:39:59,900 --> 00:40:03,597
The government gave them authority,
and they made people suffer in turn.

526
00:40:03,680 --> 00:40:06,092
Now you expect me to paint myself a hero,

527
00:40:06,360 --> 00:40:08,957
lying about solving a
problem that we created.

528
00:40:09,040 --> 00:40:12,060
This is about HQ's
credibility and dignity!

529
00:40:13,180 --> 00:40:15,360
Isho, sir, I'd be careful!

530
00:40:16,880 --> 00:40:21,097
Your egocentric actions have caused our
system of justice to lose all face today!

531
00:40:21,180 --> 00:40:23,239
If your face is all you care about,

532
00:40:23,380 --> 00:40:25,777
then you should try a little
harder to keep it clean.

533
00:40:25,860 --> 00:40:28,877
If admitting to a wrongdoing
means your trust is gone,

534
00:40:28,960 --> 00:40:32,195
then I'd say you never had
any in the first place, sir!

535
00:40:37,820 --> 00:40:41,900
You are going to clean this
entire disaster up, Fujitara.

536
00:40:42,160 --> 00:40:45,817
You will not set foot in
any naval base in the entire

537
00:40:45,900 --> 00:40:51,020
world until you bring me
Straw Hat and Law's heads.

538
00:40:51,180 --> 00:40:52,840
You understand?!

539
00:40:54,080 --> 00:40:55,440
Fine by me.

540
00:40:55,800 --> 00:40:57,340
That's just what I wanted.

541
00:40:59,340 --> 00:41:01,260
I want some meat.
